                    "fullDatabaseId": "1899856344",
                    "url": "https://github.com/BurntSushi/ripgrep/pull/2957#discussion_r1899856344",
                    "author": {
                      "login": "BurntSushi"
                    },
                    "authorAssociation": "OWNER",
                    "body": "Why are we suggesting this method? I'm okay with supporting it as long as it doesn't have any costs to doing so, but I don't see a good reason to specifically highlight it in the docs.",
                    "createdAt": "2024-12-31T00:06:19Z",
                    "lastEditedAt": null,
                    "path": "FAQ.md",
                    "diffHunk": "@@ -115,12 +115,18 @@ $ rg --generate complete-fish > \"$dir/rg.fish\"\n \n For **zsh**:\n \n-```\n+```zsh\n $ dir=\"$HOME/.zsh-complete\"\n $ mkdir -p \"$dir\"\n $ rg --generate complete-zsh > \"$dir/_rg\"\n ```\n \n+or add the following to your `.zshrc`:\n+\n+```zsh\n+$ source <(rg --generate complete-zsh) # note: this is about 4ms slower than the previous method\n+```",
                    "position": 28,
                    "originalPosition": 15,
                    "line": 129,
                    "originalLine": 128,
                    "startLine": null,
                    "originalStartLine": null,
                    "subjectType": "LINE",
                    "commit": {
                      "oid": "855bfa6cdae4f4fe8762f892fc4957635397083e"
                    },
                    "originalCommit": {
                      "oid": "1b2871720fa4ece95547a8c0c7201eb239e61ea3"
                    },
                    "replyTo": null,
                    "pullRequestReview": {
                      "id": "PRR_kwDOAzJbyc6WkPgM",
                      "fullDatabaseId": "2526083084",
                      "submittedAt": "2024-12-31T00:06:43Z"
                    }
                  },
                  {
                    "id": "PRRC_kwDOAzJbyc5xPY6v",
                    "fullDatabaseId": "1899859631",
                    "url": "https://github.com/BurntSushi/ripgrep/pull/2957#discussion_r1899859631",
                    "author": {
                      "login": "vegerot"
                    },
                    "authorAssociation": "CONTRIBUTOR",
                    "body": "Personal preference.  I personally like doing it this way because it makes installation easier.  Since the generation is fast, I don't need to think about installing `_rg` and can just put in my zshrc\r\n\r\n```zsh\r\n  if type rg > /dev/null; then\r\n\t  eval \"$(rg --generate=complete-zsh)\"\r\n  fi\r\n```\r\n\r\nI assume other people prefer it this way too, which is why projects like [fzf](https://github.com/junegunn/fzf?tab=readme-ov-file#setting-up-shell-integration) suggest it by default.  That is why I suggested it in the doc.\r\n\r\nIf you disagree, then I can remove this bit 🙂 ",
                    "createdAt": "2024-12-31T00:22:21Z",
                    "lastEditedAt": null,
                    "path": "FAQ.md",
                    "diffHunk": "@@ -115,12 +115,18 @@ $ rg --generate complete-fish > \"$dir/rg.fish\"\n \n For **zsh**:\n \n-```\n+```zsh\n $ dir=\"$HOME/.zsh-complete\"\n $ mkdir -p \"$dir\"\n $ rg --generate complete-zsh > \"$dir/_rg\"\n ```\n \n+or add the following to your `.zshrc`:\n+\n+```zsh\n+$ source <(rg --generate complete-zsh) # note: this is about 4ms slower than the previous method\n+```",
                    "position": 28,
                    "originalPosition": 15,
                    "line": 129,
                    "originalLine": 128,
                    "startLine": null,
                    "originalStartLine": null,
                    "subjectType": "LINE",
                    "commit": {
