                      "login": "okdana"
                    },
                    "authorAssociation": "CONTRIBUTOR",
                    "body": "the test script isn't wrong. the function is designed to be sourced by it without requiring anything from the completion system. we could have the script load `compdef` but it would still do the wrong thing with that check. i would suggest this as more idiomatic (and faster) than the `type` method:\r\n\r\n```zsh\r\nif [[ $funcstack[1] == _rg ]] || (( ! $+functions[compdef] )); then\r\n```",
